    </div>

    <img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0880/6173/9289/files/women-before-after-inline.png?v=1775924244" style="width:100%;max-width:560px;display:block;margin:20px auto 24px;">

    <p class="body-text">
      Dr. Maya Brooks is a renowned <strong>Black women's hair loss expert</strong>, has <strong>helped thousands of Black women stop their hair loss</strong> and reclaim their crowns — and she is an <strong>industry disruptor.</strong>
    </p>

    <p class="body-text">
      In her recent interview, she shared that a <strong>new breakthrough solution</strong> has been developed — one that targets the <em>actual root cause</em> of Black women's hair thinning and loss.
    </p>

    <p class="body-text">
      Which may <strong>effectively help stop hair loss and restore thickness, density, and edges</strong>... without any side effects of harmful pills, costly treatments, or risky procedures.
    </p>

    <p class="body-text">Here's what she told us:</p>

    <p class="quote-para">
      "For decades, I believe, the Big Hair Industry has been <strong>deliberately hiding</strong> this almost unknown condition — and its solution — from the public..."
    </p>

    <p class="quote-para">
      "This condition is known as <strong>DHT Overload Syndrome</strong> — and it is destroying Black women's hair from the inside out."
    </p>

    <p class="quote-para">
      "DHT Overload Syndrome may be the <strong>"hidden" reason</strong> why more and more Black women are suffering from severe thinning, receding edges, and bald patches — even though modern medicine has progressed massively in recent times."
    </p>

    <p class="body-text">And here's what makes it worse...</p>

    <p class="quote-para">
      "This condition is triggered — or made dramatically worse — by the hormonal changes most Black women go through at some point in their lives..."
    </p>

    <p class="quote-para">
      "Whether it's <strong>menopause</strong>, where dropping estrogen causes DHT to go unchecked and devastate follicles..."
    </p>

    <p class="quote-para">
      "Or <strong>postpartum hair loss</strong>, where the hormonal crash after pregnancy leaves hair follicles starved and shrinking..."
    </p>

    <p class="quote-para">
      "Or even <strong>hair loss from GLP-1 medications</strong> like Ozempic and Wegovy — which many women are now reporting as a major side effect..."
    </p>

    <p class="quote-para">
      "In every single one of these cases, the root driver is the same: <strong>DHT is rising, follicles are starving, and hair is falling out.</strong>"
    </p>

    <p class="body-text">What's more...</p>

    <p class="quote-para">
      "They were <strong>investing millions</strong> in keeping Black women focused on the wrong solutions — wigs, weaves, expensive salon treatments — anything to avoid talking about the real cause."
    </p>

    <p class="quote-para">
      "So <strong>Black women keep spending</strong> on products that never address what's actually happening inside their bodies."
    </p>

    <p class="body-text">But that's not all...</p>

    <p class="body-text">
      They've also been trying to <strong>take down</strong> Dr. Brooks' <strong>drug-free, all-natural solution.</strong>
    </p>

    <p class="body-text">
      She recently developed a new <strong>safe</strong>, <strong>effective</strong> and <strong>affordable</strong> natural formula — specifically for Black women.
    </p>

    <p class="body-text">
      That may <strong>quickly help reduce DHT at the source</strong> while flooding hair follicles with the nutrients they need to grow again.
    </p>

    <p class="body-text">
